<title>USA: U.S. approves GM anti-pollution spending plan.</title>
<headline>U.S. approves GM anti-pollution spending plan.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Justice Department said on Thursday that General Motors Corp. will spend more than $7 million on environmental projects to offset illegal levels of air pollution from 500,000 recalled Cadillacs.</p>
<p>The spending is part of a $45 million 1995 settlement that required the recall of the luxury cars that the department said GM fitted with devices that defeated pollution controls.</p>
<p>GM's projects include the purchase and retirement of old, polluting cars and providing electric cars, pickup trucks and shuttle buses for local communities, the department said.</p>
</text>
